From 13638f91ffd7ca9d2d4db5d426652a7c41167f7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 13:13:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02581/11362] [outer-loop] fix full-pass scorecard
 argument-order bug (explore_budget=150 -> proper budget)

The first full pass reported a false 2/25 because run_game was called with the wrong argument order:
run_game(game, explore_budget, max_exp, seed, curious) but the scorecard passed
run_game(g, 150, explore_budget, seed, max_exp) -- so explore_budget=150 (a tiny 150-expansion budget,
the literal I mistakenly passed thinking it was explore_n; run_game hard-codes n=150 internally and its
2nd arg IS the budget). Every game failed except the 3-4-action solves reachable in 150 expansions
(sp80, vc33). NOT a regression: with the correct budget, cn04@14, ar25@15, sp80@4 all solve (3/4 on the
spot-check), consistent with the prior 5/10. Corrected to run_game(g, explore_budget, max_exp, seed).
Re-running the full 25-game pass for the true accuracy scorecard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 scripts/experiments/arc3_full_pass_scorecard.py | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/experiments/arc3_full_pass_scorecard.py b/scripts/experiments/arc3_full_pass_scorecard.py
index bdbf203695..89b95ecd22 100644
--- a/scripts/experiments/arc3_full_pass_scorecard.py
+++ b/scripts/experiments/arc3_full_pass_scorecard.py
@@ -77,7 +77,8 @@ def main():
     for g in games:
         gt = time.time()
         try:
-            rec = P.run_game(g, 150, args.explore_budget, args.seed, args.max_exp)
+            # run_game(game, explore_budget, max_exp, seed, curious=True) -- pass in THAT order
+            rec = P.run_game(g, args.explore_budget, args.max_exp, args.seed)
         except Exception as ex:
             rec = {"game": g, "error": f"{type(ex).__name__}: {str(ex)[:120]}"}
         cls, actions = ("ERROR", None) if "error" in rec else classify(rec)
